CloudBurrow patch 31 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1401). Applies after patch 0030.

The gap: nothing rounds a value written to a parameterized NUMERIC(P, S)
or BIGNUMERIC(P, S) column to its scale, or refuses one with more than P
digits (2.5 and 3.5 into a NUMERIC(2, 0) read back 2.5 and 3.5). BigQuery
rounds it by the column's rounding mode and raises OUT_OF_RANGE past the
precision (https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/data-types#parameterized_decimal_type).

The patch adds the SQLite function googlesqlite_round_decimal(v,
precision, scale, mode, column), and RawSQLitePrefix: a statement
starting with it is run as SQLite SQL, so the emulator (its patch 0020)
can make, through a *sql.Tx, the triggers that call the function on each
write. round_decimal_test.go fails without the patch and passes with it.

